id: pm-gh1633
title: "GH-1633: accept comma-separated --unset field lists with per-field validation"
description: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1633\n\nReported on published 2026.10.28 in a fresh pm init --defaults workspace. pm create/update take --unset <field> once per field. A comma list such as --unset parent,release is refused as one unknown field name, and the refusal neither explains the repeat-the-flag form nor offers a corrected command. Neighbouring list flags on the same commands (--tags a,b) accept commas, so agents carry that spelling over and lose one round-trip per progressive create.\n\nThe report offers two options: (1) accept comma lists, because no field name contains a comma, validating each part and refusing unknown names one by one; (2) keep the single-field contract and add a replay correction. This item adopts option 1 if field-key validation proves commas cannot occur in a field name, and declares the flag as a list in the flag contracts so contracts, help, and recovery agree."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: agent-ux,github,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-30T12:44:36.870Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-31T01:48:58.712Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-30T13:53:30.046Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-30T13:53:30.046Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "Reproduce the reported refusal on current source and the published host; Prove field keys cannot contain commas before splitting; Accept comma lists on create, update and update-many, with every part validated and unknown or empty parts refused individually; Declare --unset as a list in flag contracts, help and docs; Cover CLI and SDK controls, including mixed repeated and comma forms, with a pre-fix negative"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: high
reporter: unbraind
severity: low
resolution: "Declared --unset as list: true on create, update and update-many. The shared parser now expands comma lists and refuses each unknown or empty part by name. schema add-field refuses comma keys and flags, which makes the split unambiguous. update many validates --unset before planning, so an unknown field no longer reports no_effect. Help (kept within the zero-headroom token ratchet), completion, the MCP description and docs describe the list form."
expected_result: "pm create/update --unset parent,release clears both fields exactly as repeated --unset flags do, and an unknown or empty part is refused by name."
actual_result: "create --unset parent,release succeeds where base refused 'parent,release'. update --unset deadline,assignee --unset release equals three repeated flags. update many dry run and apply clear comma lists. 'parnt' and empty parts are refused by name with no write. add-field 'foo,bar' is refused where base registered it. Linked tests, flag-lexicon gate 8/8 and the full suite pass."
affected_version: 2026.10.28
component: cli
