comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-30T12:44:36.870Z","harness:claude-code","Duplicate check: semantic search for --unset comma lists (top hits pm-evav, pm-ltbr, pm-hu92i3, pm-cf1u, pm-klqo, pm-kfq5, pm-nc94mk, pm-gknu, all closed), a keyword search for --unset replay corrections, and the 28 open agent-ux items. None of them owns --unset comma handling. The nearest owners are pm-gknu (closed, multi-value filter grammar) and pm-gh1626 (open, sibling same-command correction). Source report: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1633"
  "2026-10-30T13:03:38.409Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation evidence: option 1 was adopted after proving its precondition. Pre-fix, pm schema add-field \"foo,bar\" registered a comma key and advertised an unusable --foo,bar flag (reproduced on d9c4a0bca), so field keys could contain commas. normalizeAddFieldInput now refuses comma keys and comma flags, which makes the split unambiguous. --unset is declared list: true on create, update and update-many, so argv normalisation coalesces repeats and the shared parser expands comma lists (expandUnsetFieldTokens). Each part is validated and refused by name: an unknown part gives 'Unsupported --unset field \"parnt\"', an empty part gives 'must not be empty'. Separate pre-existing defect fixed in the same seam: update many --unset <unknown> exited 0 with outcome no_effect in both dry run and apply, on both pre-fix and current builds, while update refused it. The bulk preview skipped absent fields and never called the validator. A planned-update validator now refuses it before planning. The legacy dry-run test that encoded the silent acceptance of missing-field was updated. Help, zsh/fish completion, the MCP unset parameter description, COMMANDS.md and SDK.md say 'repeatable or comma-separated'. Negative control: pre-fix create --unset parent,release refused 'Unsupported --unset field \"parent,release\"'; this build creates the item."
  "2026-10-30T13:33:46.662Z","harness:claude-code","Full-suite finding, fixed before close: the flag-lexicon gate holds help-token budgets at zero headroom. The first description wording, 'Clear scalar metadata fields by name (repeatable or comma-separated)', added 4 to 5 estimated help tokens on create (1891 vs 1887), update (2079 vs 2075) and update-many (2802 vs 2797). The ratchet was not raised: the description is now 'Clear scalar fields by name (repeatable or csv)' in Commander help, both mutation option tables and zsh/fish completion. flag-lexicon-gate.spec.ts 8/8, the agent token-surface gate passes on 58 surfaces, and completion and register-commands suites pass."
